2026-09-12 | Rebalance toward full-stack, three real project galleries
- Positioning flipped to "Full-Stack Developer & Computer Vision Engineer".
  Reason from Abdullah: the front of the site read as computer vision, but the
  shipped work is mostly full-stack (platforms, business sites, e-commerce,
  automation). CV is not suppressed, it is demoted from "the practice" to "the
  differentiator". Touched: site.ts (role/title/description/availability),
  intro h1 + eyebrow, about (rewritten), capabilities (full-stack lane moved
  first), contact heading, work heading, /work copy, layout keywords,
  page.tsx knowsAbout, opengraph-image, README.
- site.stats moved to lib/stats.ts so the project count reads allWork.length
  instead of a typed number that would silently rot.
- Per-project `featured: true` replaced by an explicit FEATURED_ORDER slug list.
  The home page now leads with a platform and alternates, which the boolean
  could not express (it inherited array order), and a missing slug throws at
  build rather than silently dropping a card.
- New project: PPE Monitoring Vision System, from real screenshots. Both halves
  are his (detection + the Next.js dashboard), which is exactly the pairing the
  new positioning claims, so it sits second on the home page.
  Honesty: the figures inside those dashboards are seeded demo data. The
  headline metric stays qualitative ("Multi-site") and the gallery caption says
  so outright rather than letting 1,247 workers read as a client number.
- Real media replaced the schematic placeholders for UAV SAR and Virtual Try-On.
  The UAV "81.8 FPS" is captioned as the simulation run, not promoted to the
  headline metric, because it is not an on-aircraft figure.
- The try-on source carries a "CROGE Engineering Studio" watermark band. Cropped
  off in scripts/prepare-project-shots.mjs: it is the agency's mark, and on a
  personal portfolio it reads as someone else's work.
- Project type gained `gallery?: GalleryShot[]`, rendered only on the case-study
  page under "Inside it". Every shot carries a caption; an uncaptioned
  screenshot is decoration.
- Scroll cue moved from under the dashboard into a reserved 36px flex rail to
  its right, vertically centred, and now breathes (ci-cue-breathe, 2.8s).
  The rail is a flex sibling, not an absolute overlay, so it cannot land on the
  dashboard at any width. Measured settled at 1440x900: dashboard 541-1353,
  rail 1365-1401 (12px gap), cue centred on the rail to the pixel.
  Both cue keyframe sets end on the RESTING value, because the global
  reduced-motion rule collapses animations to 0.001ms / 1 iteration and the
  element settles on its 100% frame.

